<interrogationes unitas="pictor_componentia">

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I get pictor's component tree on screen; who calls pictor_componere?
    <responsum symbolum="pictor_componere dispensator_creare pictor_montare PictorCompositio" via="lib/pictor_applicatio.c lib/vicus_applicatio.c">You
      normally do not call it yourself: it has the dispensator's
      componere shape, so pictor_montare fills a PictorCompositio and
      pictor_applicatio passes pictor_componere and that compositio as
      ctx to dispensator_creare (vicus does the same through its
      VicusFacies). Each frame it reads the insula state and the Motus
      and returns a fresh Componens tree in the piscina it is given.
      Any of repo, piscina, intern or ctx NIHIL returns NIHIL.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I set up a PictorCompositio for a test or a new host?
    <responsum symbolum="PictorCompositio pictor_componere" via="probationes/probatio_pictor_componentia.c">memset
      the WHOLE struct to zero first (the header asks for it: ramus.repo
      NIHIL means use the repository root), then set fenestra_latitudo
      and fenestra_altitudo (the surface used until the state carries
      superficies_latitudo and superficies_altitudo), cellula_latitudo
      and cellula_altitudo (layout is in cells; 0 is treated as I),
      status_lineae (the bar height in cells) and, if you want the
      layers button and panel, doc.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quid">
    <quaestio! (>what nodes does the pictor tree contain and what are they for?
    <responsum symbolum="pictor_componere" via="probationes/pictor/pictor.arbor.stml">radix
      (action instrumentum.eligere, where keys bubble) holds prospectus
      (the clipped viewport with the pan and zoom transform), status
      (the tool bar at the bottom, a fixed number of cell lines, which
      holds the bar squares), the quadratum.strata button when a
      document is set and no paste is pending, and the open
      palette as the LAST child so it is drawn on top and hit first.
      prospectus holds tabula, the canvas, one cell in from its edge so
      the page border shows. Roles are data (ids, titles, actions), not
      per-component types; the golden tree is pictor.arbor.stml.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="cur">
    <quaestio! (>why does the canvas get its action name from the current tool instead of one handler that switches on the tool?
    <responsum symbolum="pictor_actio_instrumenti pictor_componere" via="lib/pictor_componentia.worklog.md">The
      action is chosen at compose time as a pure function of state:
      pictor_actio_instrumenti maps penicillus, aspergillum, spongia
      and linea to name.ictus and anything else to the empty string
      (no action), so handlers never branch on the tool. During a
      pending paste the canvas gets glutinatio.agere instead.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="cur">
    <quaestio! (>why is the stroke in progress copied into tabula.puncta instead of read from Motus when painting?
    <responsum symbolum="pictor_componere" via="lib/pictor_componentia.worklog.md">So
      that drawing and every figura read the tree alone (decision
      2026-09-05), and the tree snapshot shows a stroke in flight. The
      copy is made only while the mouse capture is tabula, otherwise a
      layer-row drag in the layers panel would draw a stray line.
      Previews that need more than points (spray seed and radius,
      brush diameter and colour, eraser side) are written into the
      canvas titulus as data.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how does a palette open, and how do its options know which state to change?
    <responsum symbolum="pictor_componere" via="lib/pictor_componentia.worklog.md apps/pictor/organum.stml">The
      bar squares (and quadratum.strata) carry action palette.aperire,
      which sets the transient field palette (instrumentum, color_primus,
      color_secundus, exemplar, magnitudo or strata). The composer then
      adds a PARTES_DIALOGUS node with id palette just above that
      square as the last root child. Each option of the first five is
      an optio.genus.valor square whose action is the scriptor of the
      attribute in apps/pictor/organum.stml (color_primus.ponere,
      color_secundus.ponere, instrumentum.eligere, exemplar.ponere,
      magnitudo.ponere); the current value is titled with :electum and
      the option closes the palette on click. The strata panel is
      different: oculus.id and stratum.id rows plus strata.novum and
      strata.deletum, all with action strata.agere. During a pending
      paste only the magnitudo palette can open, and the eraser's size
      square has no action, so it opens nothing.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quid">
    <quaestio! (>what squares does the pictor status bar show (the header comment lists only three)?
    <responsum symbolum="pictor_componere" via="lib/pictor_componentia.worklog.md">Five
      20 x 20 squares, a cell apart: quadratum.instrumentum,
      quadratum.color_primus, quadratum.color_secundus,
      quadratum.exemplar and quadratum.magnitudo (its title names the
      current tool's size; for spongia it is the fixed side and has no
      action). The status node's own title is the tool name, nihil when
      none. With a document set, quadratum.strata (LXX wide, titled
      strata:stratum id) sits at the right edge as a ROOT child, not a
      status child. During a pending paste the squares are replaced by
      glutinatio.A, glutinatio.B, glutinatio.confirmare and
      glutinatio.abicere (all action glutinatio.agere) plus a
      quadratum.magnitudo for the brush size. The header comment still
      describes the three-square P1a bar.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

</interrogationes>
